  "nameStory": "",
  "description": "Myrmecophilus pergandei, commonly known as the Eastern Ant Cricket, is a small cricket species belonging to the Myrmecophilidae family, characterized by its obligate association with ant colonies. These crickets have evolved specialized adaptations to live within ant nests, where they depend on their hosts for survival.",
  "idTips": [
