      "label": "Tiny Size",
      "description": "Adults are very small, typically 3-5mm in length, making them one of the smallest cricket species",
      "isPrimary": true
    },
    {
      "label": "Reduced Wings",
      "description": "Wings are highly reduced or absent, an adaptation to their subterranean nest-dwelling lifestyle",
      "isPrimary": false
    },
    {
      "label": "Pale Coloration",
      "description": "Body is typically light tan to yellowish, lacking the dark pigmentation of most surface-dwelling crickets",
      "isPrimary": false
    }
  ],
  "habitat": "Eastern Ant Crickets are found exclusively within the nests of various ant species throughout New England, living in underground or wood-based colonies where they interact closely with their host ants.",
